# Defect 016's `T?` shape (panel 230's R2, M-panic-location step 10): an `assert`
# on two fallible values wrote its expression and no side, until the sides were written as
# the specification writes the values, in the lldb formatter's notation and
# within its bounds. The line checked is the one that shows the shape.

function main()
    a: i64? = ok(3)
    b: i64? = fail(code: "nope", msg: "no value\there")
    assert a == b
